  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_006 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) at 0.653 acc, while image-only (resnet50) is very weak at 0.208 acc. Aggregation choice (avgpool vs transformer) is nearly irrelevant for RNA (0.650 vs 0.653). The critical open question is whether the image modality contributes any complementary signal when fused with the strong RNA representation, or whether it merely adds noise. This experiment (config_032: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) directly extends config_006 by adding the image branch with the simplest standard fusion (concat), isolating the effect of the image modality while holding all other design choices constant. It is the best use of the next budget slot because it answers the highest-uncertainty architectural question—whether multimodal fusion is worth the added complexity—before committing further experiments to multimodal variants. If it fails to beat 0.653, we gain strong evidence to focus on RNA-only improvements; if it helps, it validates the multimodal direction for subsequent experiments."
}

